        "root_concepts": "[network, information]",
        "section": "information-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Network Information Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Successive Interference Cancellation (SIC)**: Decode X₂ first (treating X₁ as noise),\nthen subtract X₂ and decode X₁. Achieves the corner point (I(X₁;Y|X₂), I(X₂;Y)).\nReverse order achieves the other corner. Time-sharing achieves the full capacity region boundary."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-NETWORK-INFORMATION-THEORY.md#015",
      "path": [
        "06-NETWORK-INFORMATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:information-theory:06-network-information-theory, git-history:information-theory:06-network-information-theory]",
