        "concepts": "[network, information, theory]",
        "current_path": "information-theory/06-NETWORK-INFORMATION-THEORY.md",
        "id": "maxim:information-theory:network-information-theory",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "information-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[network, information]",
        "section": "information-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Network Information Theory",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Why TDMA is suboptimal**:\n```\nTDMA: X₁ transmits fraction α, X₂ transmits (1-α)\n  R₁ = α·I(X₁;Y),  R₂ = (1-α)·I(X₂;Y)\n  Max sum = max{I(X₁;Y), I(X₂;Y)}  (convex combination)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-NETWORK-INFORMATION-THEORY.md#016",
      "path": [
        "06-NETWORK-INFORMATION-THEORY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
